Package: tunedfuzz
Title: Fuzzy String Matching with Learned Edit Costs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Pascal", "Henschke", email = "pascal.henschke@econ.lmu.de", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A weighted edit distance with multi-character edits (such as 'tz'
    read as 'ß'), exact nearest-match search under it, and edit costs learned
    from pairs of true strings and their misreadings, such as OCR, handwriting
    recognition or transcription output. The core is written in Rust and shared
    with the Python package of the same name.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/phenschke/tunedfuzz
BugReports: https://github.com/phenschke/tunedfuzz/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
